ormance of different job sectors into the feature to help models infer sectoral risk profiles.\nindustry_mean = df.groupby('Industry')['Target'].mean()  # Assuming 'Target' is the outcome variable\ndf['Industry_Target_Encoding'] = df['Industry'].map(industry_mean)", "# Group_Age_Median\n# Median for Age within Ethnicity groups.\n# Usefulness: Captures age-related trends in different ethnic groups for credit card approval patterns.\ndf['Group_Age_Median'] = df.groupby('Ethnicity')['Age'].transform('median')", "# Zscore_YearsEmployed\n# Z-score normalization of YearsEmployed.\n# Usefulness: Standardizes years of employment, making it comparable across varying scales and distributions.\ndf['Zscore_YearsEmployed'] = (df['YearsEmployed'] - df['YearsEmployed'].mean()) / df['YearsEmployed'].std()", "# Citizen_OneHot\n# One-hot encoding for Citizen feature.\n# Usefulness: Splits the Citizen categories into individual binary columns, ensuring categorical values are usable in models.\ndf = pd.get_dummies(df, columns=['Citizen'], prefix='Citizen')", "# Dropping ZipCode\ndf.drop(columns=['ZipCode'], inplace=True)", "# Dropping DriversLicense\ndf.drop(columns=['DriversLicense'], inplace=True)"]
